From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:30:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 187/342] meson_mali: buffers, the GPU's address space, lima's
 ioctls, jobs

PLAN.md M43 stage 3, the kernel side: the lima interface (Linux's request
values and layouts, headers/private/drivers/meson_mali.h) with buffers as
cloneable areas mapped into one GPU address space, contexts, sync objects
holding a job's sequence number, buffer waits, and a job thread that runs
GP and PP jobs one at a time in submission order: L2 flush, MMU zap, soft
reset, the frame (PP jobs through the broadcast window, with the load
balancer or per-PP tile lists), completion by interrupt, a 10 s timeout,
and hard resets and MMU recovery after an error. Buffers are cached for
the CPU and cleaned around jobs. Version 1.0: no growing heaps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
